        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-30T08:37:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t need a callback for the moment.\n\nAbout the vsock connection, we can handle it as a connection from the VM to the host as in the rialto test [1].\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Virtualization/rialto/tests/test.rs;l\u003d135;drc\u003d748b032fb17d902378d523505413885943cc93dc",
      "parentUuid": "d9f01f8f_352a953a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 75,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 75,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "c075a36d4360f2960a95b80c4c6b8e2d2a9eb8f6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f8edd5d3_01eec761",
        "filename": "virtualizationservice/src/service_vm.rs",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 75,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-30T09:48:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "VmInstance creates a callback \u0026 registers it with VirtMgr. I don\u0027t think there\u0027s necessarily a problem, but that code expects the callback to be invoked, which it won\u0027t be, so odd things may happen.",
      "parentUuid": "10e1cf45_3402b56d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 75,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 75,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "c075a36d4360f2960a95b80c4c6b8e2d2a9eb8f6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "03dcb277_5824d7c6",
        "filename": "virtualizationservice/src/service_vm.rs",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-29T16:13:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Something to worry about, if probably not now: What if for whatever reason we are unable to start the VM with the existing instance image? In those circumstances we should probably delete it \u0026 start again.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 81,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "c075a36d4360f2960a95b80c4c6b8e2d2a9eb8f6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c0a231d2_4fa76557",
        "filename": "virtualizationservice/src/service_vm.rs",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-30T08:37:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s a problem if we start with a new instance image in this case: Since with the new instance image pvmfw will generate a new VM secret, we will not have the same sealing CDI in the service VM to decrypt the key blob. In that case it\u0027s better to break directly here when we failed to open the existing image.",
      "parentUuid": "03dcb277_5824d7c6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 81,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "c075a36d4360f2960a95b80c4c6b8e2d2a9eb8f6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0c57a95_ee956010",
        "filename": "virtualizationservice/src/service_vm.rs",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-30T09:48:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Then you can never recover. \nGenerating a new VM secret invalidates the blob, but that will fix itself next time rkpd talks to us, won\u0027t it?",
      "parentUuid": "c0a231d2_4fa76557",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 81,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "c075a36d4360f2960a95b80c4c6b8e2d2a9eb8f6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "11781826_50d567cf",
        "filename": "virtualizationservice/src/service_vm.rs",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-30T12:00:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It depends on who starts the service VM.\n\n1. If the the client VM, then it serves nothing to use a new instance image. It will still crash later since it won\u0027t be able to decrypt any key_blob fetched from rkpd. In this case, it\u0027s better to fail early at this point.\n2. If it\u0027s rkpd, then we can take a new instance image and also invalidates all the previous keys in rkpd\u0027s pool.\n\nWe can implement 2. once we have the second the entry point for the service VM.",
      "parentUuid": "f0c57a95_ee956010",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 81,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "c075a36d4360f2960a95b80c4c6b8e2d2a9eb8f6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
